[Music]  a monarch walking freely amongst his  loyal subjects  thailand's king mahavajar along khan  greeting the people at a walkabout last  year  for a man who'd spent much of his early  reign outside thailand  it was part of a new engagement to bring  him closer to his people  for ordinary ties it's part of a  familiar routine  i've been taught to love the king since  i was young i grew up with phrases like  long live the king or i love the king  i grew up watching news about the  monarchy's household i learned about the  institution in school  people around me loved the king but then  i wondered why do we love the king  benja now rejects many of the official  histories she was taught as a child  as do other young thais who are calling  for reforms  protesters have taken to the streets  demanding the royal household be more  transparent  and accountable for many ties it marked  a huge change  ideas that were only discussed in  private are now being talked about in  public  but when protesters moved against the  crown property bureau  the office that manages the king's  enormous wealth  they found the streets blocked with  shipping containers  when they moved towards the palace they  were met with tear gas and rubber  bullets  protest leaders have been arrested and  charged with less majesty  the offense of insulting the monarchy  that comes with a lengthy jail term  since then the protests have largely  died out  that say pro-monarchists is evidence  that most thai people  have seen through the protests as an  attack on the institution  the protesters want to abolish not  reform  don't forget the demands that they've  been asking for are deliberately aiming  to bring down the monarchy  not to help improve the institution so  it's not surprising that not many people  come out to support them  on the occasion of the king's 69th  birthday there's unlikely to be much  pomp  or ceremony this year with cobit  restrictions in place  official celebrations of the king's  birthday are likely to be very muted  but many people think once those  restrictions are lifted  protesters calling for reform of the  monarchy  could hit the streets once again in  recent months the king has stayed out of  the public eye  when he's been seen he's relied on the  queen for support  and despite his position of power he  appears to be a monarch  unsure of his relationship with his  subjects  tony chang al jazeera bangkok

